    description: "Found in DEEP bakeoff deep-20260623-134237 cohort-001 iter-004 (zoxide, Rust CLI). The Rust call graph leaves the subcommand tree as disconnected islands: main()'s 'Cmd::parse().run()' resolves '.run()' to an external stub ('rust:external:0-0:run:external_symbol') even though 'Cmd.run:method' exists as a node; 'Cmd.run' has 0 outgoing edges (the match-arm 'cmd.run()' calls are dropped); and all six variant '.run()' methods have 0 incoming calls. Broadly, 404/589 (69%) of Rust 'calls' edges land on external/unresolved stubs, so the forward slice from main() reaches only 4 nodes and never enters the subcommand handlers. Distinct from the adjacent DONE items WI-gahuk (cross-file call resolution) and WI-tulid (trait-impl relationship EDGES) — this is trait-METHOD-CALL dispatch through enum match arms + trait objects not resolving to the in-tree impl. Evidence: reflect/cohort-001/iter-004/zoxide.assessment.yaml; slice.0.json (4 nodes from main)."  # 8bbc
